name:        Challenge: Interrupting a substantial APNG export leaves no partial download and allows a later export
type:        frontend
createdFrom: cli
status:      failed
priority:    Medium
planSteps:   14
  1. [action] Navigate to /studio.
  2. [assertion] Verify restoration has finished and the main drawing canvas is editable.
  3. [action] Open File, then Canvas size… and resize to 256 by 256 with Scale Artwork enabled; apply the resize.
  4. [action] Select the Pen tool.
  5. [action] Draw a short horizontal stroke in the upper-left quarter of the drawing canvas, away from its borders.
  6. [action] Use Frame actions, Duplicate frame repeatedly to produce 24 frames.
  7. [assertion] Verify exactly 24 frames exist and the current frame still contains the horizontal stroke.
  8. [action] Open Export drawing and select APNG at 2x scale.
  9. [action] Click Download APNG and press Escape immediately while Encoding APNG progress is active.
  10. [assertion] Verify the export dialog closes and no APNG download completes for the cancelled operation. If encoding completed before cancellation could happen, report this case blocked rather than passing it.
  11. [assertion] Verify all 24 frames and the original stroke remain intact.
  12. [action] Open Export drawing and select PNG at 1x scale.
  13. [action] Click Download PNG.
  14. [assertion] Verify a nonempty PNG downloads and opens as the original 256 by 256 drawing; a filename without a completed file is insufficient.
